  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 750eb (Expensive) <strong>♦</strong> <strong>Required Slots:</strong> 1</p>\n<p><strong>Fits:</strong> All Assault Rifles, Sniper Rifles, and Shotguns that use detachable magazines (e.g., double barrel shotguns are not compatible) and do not have an equipped Belt Box or Backpack Magazine</p>\n<p><em>Two is usually better than one. At least, for big guns anyway.</em></p>\n<p>While the weapon’s magazine is empty, and the user is holding/wielding the weapon in two hands, they can sacrifice their Move Action to Reload the weapon without an Action. The Mag Coupler is then considered expended, and cannot be used again until an Action is used to reset it. The weapon can still be reloaded normally with the Reload Action while the Mag Coupler is expended. While installed, the weapon cannot be concealed or installed as a Popup Weapon.</p>\n<p><strong>Attachment slots:</strong> 1</p>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Weapons &gt; Attachment Catalog &gt; Capacity &amp; Reloading).</em></p>"
